"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. The project has progressed through several phases: initial findings in August highlighted a potential 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms; the team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture; the design phase was completed, leading to a development phase led by Omar Jensen; a milestone celebrating the completion of the testing phase was reached in October; and phase two progress in November reported a breakthrough in predictive analytics. Strategic partnerships with TechInnovate were explored and eventually secured to leverage AI technology. Additionally, feedback is being sought on the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November, and there is an urgent request regarding a project chart and confirmation to be sent to Catherine."
